y is diffuse.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186, 639, 1818],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"1385 fires exactly once (bucket [74149,74748]) and only into hub 639; 1186 is touched exactly once, only by 1818. Since 639 is not an in-neighbour of 1818, the minimal route is 1385->639->X->1818->1186, needing three consecutive <=600-unit relays confined to ~[74149,76000]. No evidence supports events in that narrow band; the apparent connectivity comes entirely from 639's hub status in the time-ignoring 2-hop graph, and per-node activity is only ~3 events over a 38k-unit span, so a tight legal chain is not supported.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 20429, "total_output_tokens": 6772, "total_tokens": 27201, "total_latency_ms": 90018, "llm_calls": 4, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}